Pick the ICU package that a secondary architecture actually has

The secondary-architecture package list in the top-level Jamfile asks for "icu"
unconditionally. On an x86_gcc2 hybrid the secondary architecture is plain x86,
whose ICU package in the pinned HaikuPorts snapshot is icu74_x86 -- there is no
icu_x86 -- so the image target cannot be made:

    AddHaikuImagePackages: package icu not available!
    ...skipped 20 target(s)...

and no anyboot ISO is produced. The build otherwise completes: 19624 targets
update, and jam reports no failing action, which is what makes this one slow to
find. The message names the package but not the caller; adding the calling
context to build/jam/ImageRules is what identified it:

    [dir= system packages ] [arch= x86 ] [list= freetype icu zlib ]

DefaultBuildProfiles already spells the same choice correctly for the bootstrap
profile ("icu@gcc2 icu74@!gcc2"), so use that here. For an x86_gcc2 hybrid the
secondary arch is not gcc2 and gets icu74_x86; a gcc2 architecture still gets
icu.

Verified against 4b0e529517 (r1beta6): with this change the nightly-anyboot
profile builds to completion and the resulting image boots to a desktop under
QEMU with four vCPUs.

This is independent of the VAIO P patch set -- reverting that patch leaves the
failure unchanged.

diff --git a/Jamfile b/Jamfile
index 3aaf1e6d58..8d634521f7 100644
--- a/Jamfile
+++ b/Jamfile
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@ if $(HAIKU_PACKAGING_ARCHS[2]) {
 			in [ MultiArchSubDirSetup $(HAIKU_PACKAGING_ARCHS[2-]) ] {
 		on $(architectureObject) {
 			AddHaikuImageSystemPackages [ FFilterByBuildFeatures
-				freetype icu zlib
+				freetype icu@gcc2 icu74@!gcc2 zlib

 				regular_image @{
 					ffmpeg6 glu jasper jpeg libavif libicns libpng16 libwebp mesa
